            <fr:title text="The running max makes the chunk merge exact">The running max makes the chunk merge exact</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1787063263978</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p>In <fr:link href="/R0PM/" title="Flash Attention (v1)" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/R0PM/" display-uri="R0PM" type="local">flash attention</fr:link>, what running statistics travel between KV chunks, and how are two chunks merged?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  Each query block carries three: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[M]]></fr:tex>, the running maximum of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q \cdot  k]]></fr:tex>; <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[L]]></fr:tex>, the running <fr:link href="/C00V/" title="Softmax" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/C00V/" display-uri="C00V" type="local">softmax</fr:link> denominator; and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[O]]></fr:tex>, the running output.

  Merging chunks with local maxima <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[M^1, M^2]]></fr:tex> and sums <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[L^1, L^2]]></fr:tex> rescales each to the shared maximum:

  <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[L = e^{M^1 - \max (M^1, M^2)}L^1 + e^{M^2 - \max (M^1, M^2)}L^2]]></fr:tex>

  <html:strong>This is exact, not an approximation.</html:strong> It is only <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\sum _i e^{a_i + b} = e^b \sum _i e^{a_i}]]></fr:tex>: pulling a constant out of a sum of exponentials. The maximum is subtracted for <fr:link href="/7TMH/" title="Stabilizing Softmax in Attention" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/7TMH/" display-uri="7TMH" type="local">numerical stability</fr:link> and put back by the same identity — see <fr:link href="/PI7N/" title="Online Softmax" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/PI7N/" display-uri="PI7N" type="local">Online Softmax</fr:link> for the one-pass version of the argument.

  <html:strong>The payoff is memory, not FLOPs.</html:strong> The <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[[B,T,S,N]]]></fr:tex> attention matrix is never materialised, so memory is <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[O(1)]]></fr:tex> in the number of chunks while the FLOP count stays quadratic. The query block sits in <fr:link href="/GFK2/" title="VMEM" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/GFK2/" display-uri="GFK2" type="local">VMEM</fr:link> and only the KV chunks stream in, which is also what raises the <fr:link href="/YBQD/" title="Arithmetic intensity" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/YBQD/" display-uri="YBQD" type="local">arithmetic intensity</fr:link>.
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
